9. How Do You Version APIs?
What Interviewer Wants to Know

Can APIs evolve without breaking existing consumers?

URI Versioning
/api/v1/customer
/api/v2/customer


Most widely used approach.

Header Versioning
Accept: application/vnd.customer.v2


Often seen in enterprise environments.

Best Practices
Maintain Backward Compatibility
Avoid Breaking Changes
Deprecate Gradually
Communicate API Changes

Interview Answer

"I use URI or header-based versioning and ensure backward compatibility so existing clients continue to work without modification."

10. How Do You Deploy Microservices Without Downtime?
What Interviewer Wants to Know

Can you release software safely in production?

Rolling Deployment
Pod 1 → Updated
Pod 2 → Updated
Pod 3 → Updated


One instance updated at a time.

Blue-Green Deployment
Blue  = Current Version
Green = New Version


Traffic switches instantly.

Canary Deployment
5%
10%
25%
50%
100%


Traffic gradually shifts to the new release.

Kubernetes Features
Deployment
ReplicaSet
Readiness Probe
Liveness Probe
HPA

Interview Answer

"I use rolling, blue-green, or canary deployments with Kubernetes readiness probes to achieve zero-downtime deployments and minimize release risks."

